::CW_U05_L01_GP_Q01::Draft excerpt: I walked into the room. It was weird. Something felt different. Feedback: I cannot picture the room. Which revision goal is best?{
~A. Change every sentence because the draft is bad.#Incorrect. Revision should be targeted, not random.
~B. Delete the whole draft and start over.#Incorrect. The feedback names a specific issue, so a targeted revision is better.
=
~D. Add a new character with no connection to the room.#Incorrect. That does not solve the setting problem.
}

::CW_U05_L01_GP_Q02::Draft excerpt: The poem is about missing my old neighborhood. Feedback: Add one concrete image from the neighborhood. Which revision best uses the feedback?{
=
~B. Add a sentence saying the poem is emotional.#Incorrect. That tells feeling but does not add a concrete image.
~C. Remove all details about the neighborhood.#Incorrect. That works against the feedback.
~D. Change the poem into a research report.#Incorrect. The feedback asks for an image, not a new genre.
}

::CW_U05_L01_GP_Q03::Feedback: Make it better. How should this feedback be classified?{
~A. Specific and actionable.#Incorrect. It does not identify what needs improvement.
=
~C. A clear revision goal.#Incorrect. It is too general to be a goal.
~D. A convention correction.#Incorrect. It does not mention grammar, punctuation, or spelling.
}

::CW_U05_L01_GP_Q04::Online suggestion: Replace your sentence with a more formal sentence that removes the narrator's voice. The draft is a first-person memoir. What should the writer do?{
~A. Accept it automatically because online tools are always right.#Incorrect. Online tools may not understand creative voice.
~C. Delete the memoir.#Incorrect. The suggestion does not require deleting the piece.
~D. Ignore all online feedback forever.#Incorrect. Some online feedback can be useful.
=
}

::CW_U05_L01_GP_Q05::Draft excerpt: The ending feels sudden. Peer feedback: Add one sentence showing the character deciding to leave. Which revision best fits?{
~B. The sky was blue yesterday.#Incorrect. This does not show the character deciding to leave.
~C. My favorite food is soup.#Incorrect. This is unrelated.
=
~D. Everyone lived happily forever with no reason.#Incorrect. This does not address the sudden ending.
}
